        "original_id": "7b3f0196-5784-5277-a611-1426e6eede56",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Denys Lionel Page\n- Organizations: British Academy\n- Places: Reading, Berkshire; Tarset; Oxford, England\n- Universities: University of Oxford; University of Cambridge\n- Roles: British classical scholar; President of the British Academy\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Oxford is a collegiate research university located in Oxford, England.\n- The University of Oxford has evidence of teaching dating back to 1096, making it the oldest university in the English-speaking world and the world's second-oldest university in continuous operation.\n- Denys Lionel Page was born on 11 May 1908 in Reading, Berkshire.\n- Denys Lionel Page was a British classical scholar at the University of Oxford and the University of Cambridge.\n- Denys Lionel Page served as President of the British Academy from 1971 to 1974.\n- Denys Lionel Page died on 6 July 1978 in Tarset.",
